### Job Service

#### [MODIFY] [jobService.js](file:///d:/new/Odito/odito_backend/src/modules/jobs/service/jobService.js)

Add `createAndDispatchTechnicalDomainJob(linkDiscoveryJob)` method. Pattern mirrors [createAndDispatchPageScrapingJob()](file:///d:/new/Odito/odito_backend/src/modules/jobs/service/jobService.js#555-594) but simpler — passes `projectId` and `domain` (extracted from `input_data.main_url`) as input data.

---

### Job Dispatcher

#### [MODIFY] [jobDispatcher.js](file:///d:/new/Odito/odito_backend/src/modules/jobs/service/jobDispatcher.js)

Add `dispatchTechnicalDomainJob(job)` method — HTTP POST to `${pythonBaseURL}/api/jobs/technical-domain` with `{ jobId, projectId, userId, domain }`. Timeout: 60s.

---

### Pipeline Chaining (Critical)

#### [MODIFY] [jobController.js](file:///d:/new/Odito/odito_backend/src/modules/jobs/controller/jobController.js)

**LINK_DISCOVERY completion (lines ~60–96)**: Change to create `TECHNICAL_DOMAIN` job instead of `PAGE_SCRAPING`.

```diff
- const pageScrapingJob = await jobService.createAndDispatchPageScrapingJob(updatedJob);
+ const technicalDomainJob = await jobService.createAndDispatchTechnicalDomainJob(updatedJob);
```

Stage emit: `from: 'LINK_DISCOVERY', to: 'TECHNICAL_DOMAIN'`

**Add new `TECHNICAL_DOMAIN` completion handler**: After the existing `LINK_DISCOVERY` block, add a new `else if` for `JOB_TYPES.TECHNICAL_DOMAIN`. On completion, create and dispatch `PAGE_SCRAPING` job (copy the existing pattern from the old LINK_DISCOVERY handler). This preserves the full pipeline chain.

> [!IMPORTANT]
> If `TECHNICAL_DOMAIN` fails, the pipeline must still proceed to `PAGE_SCRAPING`. The failure handler in [failJob](file:///d:/new/Odito/odito_backend/src/modules/jobs/service/jobService.js#234-282) should also create `PAGE_SCRAPING` as a fallback.

#### [MODIFY] [jobCompletionHandler.js](file:///d:/new/Odito/odito_backend/src/modules/jobs/controller/jobCompletionHandler.js)

Same changes applied to the async completion handler:
1. [handleLinkDiscoveryCompletion](file:///d:/new/Odito/odito_backend/src/modules/jobs/controller/jobCompletionHandler.js#181-220) → create `TECHNICAL_DOMAIN` instead of `PAGE_SCRAPING`
2. Add `handleTechnicalDomainCompletion` → create `PAGE_SCRAPING`
3. Update [chainNextJobs](file:///d:/new/Odito/odito_backend/src/modules/jobs/controller/jobCompletionHandler.js#140-180) switch to include `JOB_TYPES.TECHNICAL_DOMAIN`
4. Update [createNextJobAtomically](file:///d:/new/Odito/odito_backend/src/modules/jobs/controller/jobCompletionHandler.js#16-67) switch to include `JOB_TYPES.TECHNICAL_DOMAIN`

