### Python API Router

#### [NEW] [technical_domain.py](file:///d:/new/Odito/python_workers/api/technical_domain.py)

FastAPI router at `POST /api/jobs/technical-domain`. Pydantic model: `TechnicalDomainJob(jobId, projectId, userId, domain)`. Calls `execute_technical_domain` worker function.

#### [MODIFY] [main.py](file:///d:/new/Odito/python_workers/main.py)

Register the new router:
```python
from api.technical_domain import router as technical_domain_router
app.include_router(technical_domain_router, prefix="/api", tags=["technical_domain"])
```

---

### Python Worker

#### [NEW] `scraper/workers/seo/technical_domain/` folder

| File | Purpose |
|------|---------|
| [__init__.py](file:///d:/new/Odito/python_workers/scraper/__init__.py) | Package init |
| [worker.py](file:///d:/new/Odito/python_workers/scraper/workers/ai/ai_scoring_v2/ai_scoring_v2_worker.py) | Orchestrator: fetches robots + sitemap, stores via backend API, reports completion |
| `robots_fetcher.py` | `fetch_robots(domain)` → `{ status, exists, content }` |
| `sitemap_fetcher.py` | `fetch_sitemap(domain)` → `{ status, exists, content, urlCount }` |

**Key behaviors:**
- HTTP GET to `domain/robots.txt` and `domain/sitemap.xml` with 10s timeout
- On fetch failure: log error, return default empty result (never raise)
- Store results via `POST /api/domain-technical-report` to Node.js backend
- Report job completion via `POST /api/jobs/{jobId}/complete`
- Always returns success status so pipeline continues

---

