## API Contract

### Node → Python (Dispatch)
```
POST http://127.0.0.1:8000/api/jobs/technical-domain
{
  "jobId": "string",
  "projectId": "string",
  "userId": "string",
  "domain": "string"   // e.g. "https://example.com"
}
```

### Python → Node (Store Report)
```
POST http://localhost:5000/api/jobs/domain-technical-report
{
  "projectId": "string",
  "domain": "string",
  "robotsStatus": 200,
  "robotsExists": true,
  "robotsContent": "...",
  "sitemapStatus": 200,
  "sitemapExists": true,
  "sitemapContent": "...",
  "parsedSitemapUrlCount": 45
}
```

### Python → Node (Job Completion)
```
POST http://localhost:5000/api/jobs/{jobId}/complete
{
  "stats": {
    "robotsExists": true,
    "sitemapExists": true,
    "parsedSitemapUrlCount": 45
  }
}
```

## Safety Confirmation

| Concern | Status |
|---------|--------|
| Scoring logic untouched | ✅ No changes to scoring files |
| Rule engine untouched | ✅ No changes to rules/ |
| Performance logic untouched | ✅ No changes to performance workers |
| Architecture preserved | ✅ Same PUSH model, same chaining pattern |
| Pipeline continues on failure | ✅ Fallback to PAGE_SCRAPING on TECHNICAL_DOMAIN failure |

## Verification Plan

### Manual Verification
Since there are no existing automated tests in this codebase, verification will be manual:

1. **Static review**: Verify all modified files compile/parse without errors
2. **Pipeline chain integrity**: Trace the chain `LINK_DISCOVERY → TECHNICAL_DOMAIN → PAGE_SCRAPING` through both [jobController.js](file:///d:/new/Odito/odito_backend/src/modules/jobs/controller/jobController.js) and [jobCompletionHandler.js](file:///d:/new/Odito/odito_backend/src/modules/jobs/controller/jobCompletionHandler.js) to confirm no broken paths
3. **Failure resilience**: Confirm that [failJob](file:///d:/new/Odito/odito_backend/src/modules/jobs/service/jobService.js#234-282) handler creates `PAGE_SCRAPING` as fallback when `TECHNICAL_DOMAIN` fails
4. **No scoring contamination**: `grep` for any references to scoring, rules, or performance in the new code to confirm zero contamination

> [!NOTE]
> Full end-to-end testing requires running both Node.js and Python servers with a MongoDB instance. I recommend you test this after deployment by triggering an audit on a test project.
